    "field": "Climate science",
    "problem": "Climate models overestimate observed global warming on decadal scales like the \"global warming hiatus,\" and studies quantifying the role of Pacific variability in this discrepancy yield widely divergent results, with estimated contributions differing by a factor of five.",
    "method": "This paper reconciles observed and modelled global temperatures by adjusting multi-model ensemble means for Pacific variability, after first removing the externally forced warming signal from the tropical Pacific sea surface temperature record to isolate the internal variability component.",
    "task": "The task is to investigate the role of equatorial Pacific variability in reconciling the divergences between observed and modelled global mean temperature increases since 1950 by comparing multiple studies and methods.",
